Reason: port: with frame_rate = 60 the plaza gates' calc-anim swirl state (wind timer, close rate) steps once per 1/30 s as at 30; stepping it every frame cancels the per-tick opening rate, so an already-open gate (every re-entry to Bianco Hills, Ricco Harbor, Gelato Beach, ...) never opens; on the skipped frames the swirl's keep-alive particle requests are still made, since the particle manager kills a type-1 emitter that is not re-requested on its next pass
--- a/src/MoveBG/ModelGate.cpp
+++ b/src/MoveBG/ModelGate.cpp
@@ -29,6 +29,27 @@
 #include <MSound/MSSetSound.hpp>
 #include <MSound/MSoundBGM.hpp>
 
+#ifdef TARGET_PC
+#include <System/MarDirector.hpp>
+
+// Port: with frame_rate = 60, TMarDirector::direct still runs CUE_MOVE in
+// 1/120 s ticks (two a frame instead of four) but CUE_CALC_ANIM comes every
+// frame, twice as often per second as at 30. Near an open gate, perform's
+// movement pass adds 0.01 to mOpenRate per tick and, while the wind is out,
+// the calc pass takes mCloseSpeed (0.02) off per call: +0.04 against -0.02
+// per 1/30 s at 30, but +0.02 against -0.02 per frame at 60, so a gate that
+// is already open (every gate after its first use) never swirls up, the wind
+// never starts, and Mario cannot jump in. The swirl's state (wind timer,
+// close rates) is gameplay, so step it once per 1/30 s: on the calc pass of
+// every other frame at 60 (the director counts one unk5C per tick, two a
+// frame). The animation frame is still set on every pass.
+extern "C" int port_fps60_active;
+static inline bool ModelGatePortCalcStep()
+{
+	return !port_fps60_active || (gpMarDirector->unk5C & 2) != 0;
+}
+#endif
